.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-snapshot-delete 1  "tapectl-snapshot-delete " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-snapshot\-delete \- Delete an unwritten snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl snapshot delete\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-version\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete an unwritten snapshot
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Snapshot version to delete
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Force delete even if staged (but not written)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Unit name
